-- The only `i64.div_s` that engine-traps is INT64_MIN / -1, and INT64_MIN is -2^63,
-- NOT intMinBound (-2^62).  The one way to reach it is a dividend built by an ADD
-- that overflows to exactly -2^63: `intMinBound + intMinBound`.  Since #3377 that add
-- is itself the coded E-INT-OVERFLOW trap, so the divide is never reached and no
-- uncoded engine trap ("divide result unrepresentable") can occur.
-- expect-stderr: runtime error [E-INT-OVERFLOW]: (-4611686018427387904) + (-4611686018427387904) overflows Int
main = (0 - 4611686018427387903 - 1 + (0 - 4611686018427387903 - 1)) / (0 - 1)
